# PLAN-1083 — AV 名义类型、枚举载荷与标量判别（语言共享语料 types 面）

The canonical author of the variants/types language family. Every case
carries ONE Auto source; the `av` check runs the ordinary AV language
chain (`ac-av/language-source-run-v1`); legacy `VM result`/`VM stdout`
checks keep their original oracles and owners with the AV-phase `#ignore`
marker (AV-ONLY-1078-1096) — not executed in this phase, never blocking
the AV gate; their backend tasks remove the marker when they land.

Auditable normalizations (recorded per row in
`language/migration/legacy-map.tsv`, same policy as PLAN-1082's fn-main
wrapping and PLAN-1081's typed-lambda annotations):

- Legacy fn-local `enum` declarations (09_functions.016..019) hoist to
  module scope in the canonical spelling — the enum names are distinct
  and capture-free; the legacy local spelling stays the row's original
  oracle in the map.
- Legacy `enum Color { Red = 1, Green = 2 }` comma separators parse on
  this face (PLAN-1083 arm-comma absorption); the canonical keeps the
  legacy spelling byte-for-byte.
- Legacy str-returning `is` expressions (10_types.011/012: `1 -> "red"`)
  normalize to int-coded arms (red→10, green→20, blue→30, unknown→0) —
  the printed digits map 1:1 onto the legacy words; the legacy word
  oracle stays the row's original oracle.
- Method receivers are read-only views on this face: legacy field-WRITE
  methods (m01 `inc`/`set_to`, m08 setters, m09 `set`) are held for the
  borrows batch (AVP-08 `&mut self` seam); the READ faces (get, chained
  reads, method-values) are asserted green here.
- `.helper(3)` implicit-self method calls normalize to the explicit
  `self.helper(3)` (identical semantics; the legacy implicit spelling
  stays in the frozen row).

## Case: named-enum-payload
id: "av.parity.1083.named-enum-payload"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1083", "types"]
links: ["PLAN-1083"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
enum Answer { Yes { code int, text Str }; No }
fn main() int {
 let a = Answer.Yes(code: 42, text: "ok")
 is a { Answer.Yes(code, text) -> { if text == "ok" { return code }; return 0 }; Answer.No -> { return 0 } }
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 42

### Notes

§6 contract case 1: a NAMED multi-field payload — declaration, named
construction (in order), multi-binding destructuring and the bare arm in
one program. The §6 draft verbatim; landed byte-for-byte.

